        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.071,
            0.494,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.111,
            0.859,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.1.1 Standard Form of Linear Equations in Two Variables"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.143,
            0.881,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Any equation that can be expressed in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where a, b and c are real numbers, and a and b are not both zero, is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear equation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in two variables."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.2,
            0.882,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is referred to as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "standard form",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the linear equation. Here a and b are the coefficients of the variables x and y respectively and c is a constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.263,
            0.505,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is useful to note the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.283,
            0.882,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The coefficients a and b and the constant c can also be rational numbers. For example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{4}x + \\frac{3}{5}y - \\frac{1}{2} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is also a linear equation in two variables in standard form. However, for convenience, in such cases we often multiply the equation by a suitable number to remove the fractions and write the equation with integer coefficients. Here we can multiply by 20 to get the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x + 12y - 10 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.432,
            0.881,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Equations of the type "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are special cases of linear equations in two variables as they can be expressed as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax+0×y+c=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . For example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 + 4x = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4x + 0 \\times y + 7 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 4,   b = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and c = 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.519,
            0.88,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Write each of the following equations in standard form, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "ax + by + c = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and indicate the values of a, b and c in each case:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.562,
            0.867,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x + 2y = 2.7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{3}{2}y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 = 1 . 5 x - 1 . 3 y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.593,
            0.308,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 y = 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.624,
            0.263,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.648,
            0.881,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x + 2y = 2.7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x + 2y - 2.7 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 5 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = - 2 . 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The equation can also be rewritten as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-5x-2y+2.7=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . In this case "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a=-5,   b=-2,   c=2.7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.714,
            0.685,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { x } { 2 } \\div 4 = \\frac { 3 } { 2 } y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}y-4=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = \\frac{1}{2}, b = -\\frac{3}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = -   4 ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.786,
            0.881,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 = 1 . 5 x - 1 . 3 y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1.5x - 1.3y - 4 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 1.5,   b = -1.3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = - 4 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It can also be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-1.5x + 1.3y + 4 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . In this case "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = -1.5, b = 1.3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.851,
            0.881,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) 3y = 5 can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 \\times x + 3y - 5 = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Here "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 0,   b = 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = - 5 ."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
